# General Project Rules

## Tech Stack

- React Native with Expo Router (file-based routing)
- TypeScript (strict mode)
- NativeWind v4 (Tailwind CSS for React Native)
- TanStack Query v5 (data fetching)
- TanStack Form v1 (form handling)
- Zustand (state management)
- i18next (internationalization)
- Biome (linting/formatting)
- Jest (testing)
- Storybook (component documentation)

## Directory Structure

- `app/` - Expo Router pages (file-based routing)
- `components/` - UI components (atoms/molecules/organisms/templates)
- `domain/` - Business logic, service interfaces, types
- `gateway/` - External interface implementations (REST, storage, etc.)
- `context/` - React Context providers
- `i18n/` - Translation files
- `lib/` - Shared utilities and helpers

## File Naming Conventions

- Components: PascalCase (e.g., `LoginForm.tsx`)
- Services: camelCase (e.g., `authService.ts`)
- Types: PascalCase (e.g., `User.ts`)
- Tests: `.test.ts` or `.test.tsx`
- Stories: `.stories.tsx`
- Index files: `index.ts` for exports

## Import/Export Patterns

- Use path aliases: `~/` for root directory
- Export from domain via `domain/index.ts`
- Export components via `index.ts` in component directories
- Prefer named exports over default exports

## Common Utilities

- `lib/utils.ts` - General utilities
- `lib/colors.ts` - Color system
- `lib/featureFlag.ts` - Feature flag helpers
- `lib/useColorScheme.tsx` - Theme detection

## Development Workflow

- Run `npm run lint` before committing
- Run `npm run test:watch` for development
- Run `npm run test:ci` for CI
- Generate API types: `npm run generate:api-types`
- Storybook: `npm run storybook-generate`

## Backward Compatibility

- **No backward compatibility required** - The app is not in production, so breaking changes are acceptable when updating features or APIs
- Focus on implementing the best solution rather than maintaining compatibility with existing code

## Key Dependencies Usage

- React Native: Core framework
- Expo Router: Navigation and routing
- NativeWind: Styling with Tailwind classes
- TanStack Query: Server state management
- TanStack Form: Form state and validation
- Zustand: Client state management
- i18next: Translation system
- Zod: Schema validation
